# Database migrations

Do **not** run migrations unless the user explicitly asks you to run them in that message.

This includes:

- Local: `alembic upgrade`, `alembic stamp`, `alembic downgrade` against any real database (the local `.env` `DATABASE_URL` points at prod)
- Remote: `heroku run alembic …` or any hosted one-off migration command
- Applying schema changes directly via SQL against production or shared databases

Allowed without asking: `python scripts/check_migrations.py`, which only touches the throwaway Postgres it creates.

When schema changes are part of a task:

- Update `db/models.py` and add an Alembic revision in `migrations/versions/` using `migrations/helpers.py` (guarded, re-runnable; forward-only; revision id at most 32 characters)
- Run `python scripts/check_migrations.py`
- Tell the user what the revision does; deploying applies it (Heroku release phase runs `alembic upgrade head`). Do not deploy or push unless asked

If ingest or deploy errors are likely due to a missing migration, diagnose from logs, explain the fix, and give the exact command for the user to run.
